      "writtenOn": "2024-04-18T08:25:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So it sounds like, before this modification, there will be call state change executed twice - is that correct?\n\n - first at HfpCallbak receiving AT command\n - second time at dispatch UHID output\n \nThat would cause desync regardless of network stability. Can you help confirm?\n\nIf so then we should focus on eliminating all these possible \"double phone ops\" in bluetooth_media.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "3599c7de179a9273298b30b9d1694167e6ed110a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff11fcea_c3fc40d5",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 2012120
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T08:44:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The primary issue is not the occurrence of \"double phone ops.\"\n\nThe actual problem arises when the HfpCallback receives an AT command, but the VC app does not receive the headset event due to network instability. So if the first attempt to answer the call is unsuccessful(due to an event that does not propagate correctly to the central web server) , the user is unable to re-answer the call on the second attempt because the call state is already changed when receiving an AT command.\n\nEven in current code, call state change will only change once. The major difference of this change is that we want to change the call state at \n* at dispatch UHID output\n* instead of at HfpCallbak receiving AT command\n\nAnd the `at dispatch UHID output` is better since that is the moment VC app confirm the phone_state change on their side.",
      "parentUuid": "3cc254a2_bcf97c0a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "3599c7de179a9273298b30b9d1694167e6ed110a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9300b948_91cfa191",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 2012120
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T08:57:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also the implementation here is actually not the same like we write in design doc.\n\nThe design doc change the call state after receive UHID output instead of receiving AT command",
      "parentUuid": "ff11fcea_c3fc40d5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "3599c7de179a9273298b30b9d1694167e6ed110a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6fcd02e3_ac8e4e43",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1079709
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-24T08:39:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let me reword a bit.\n\nAccording to the base patchset, call state change was arranged at two places - (a) at HfpCallback and (b) at dispatch UHID output. \n\nAnd that is the typical problem: when some respect (a) and others respect (b), it becomes state out-of-sync - and which is a pretty big issue.\n\nI was trying to point out here that, \"Unable to re-answer\" is just one example of this bigger out-of-sync problem.\n\nHighly suggest you use a proper fix to address the fundamental out-of-sync problem for good.",
      "parentUuid": "9300b948_91cfa191",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "3599c7de179a9273298b30b9d1694167e6ed110a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c3a732ce_4b7e7fd6",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 2012120
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-24T09:57:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks to point it out the fundamental problem here.\n\nTo properly fix it, the fundamental out-of-sync problem can all be fixed by a similar approach in HFP callback. I can review HFP callback and see what function needs to be changed with the same method.",
